WEBVTT

00:00:03.083 --> 00:00:05.750
AI is reshaping how we build data centers.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.916
With computational demands
quadrupling yearly, physical racks

00:00:09.916 --> 00:00:13.500
are now pushing towards
200 kilowatts on the way to one megawatt.

00:00:13.916 --> 00:00:18.833
Power, cooling, and spatial design
are no longer isolated considerations.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.291
They’ve become one
interdependent challenge.

00:00:22.958 --> 00:00:25.791
Traditional racks relied on air
cooling and distributed

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:30.125
power components,
but that approach doesn’t scale.

00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:35.041
Today’s AI-ready racks integrate liquid
cooling, centralized power distribution,

00:00:35.041 --> 00:00:38.375
and high-voltage DC to boost density,

00:00:38.458 --> 00:00:41.916
reclaim internal space,
and improve energy efficiency.

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:45.041
Cooling begins at the component level.

00:00:45.041 --> 00:00:48.291
From cold plates
to immersion tanks, these solutions

00:00:48.291 --> 00:00:54.041
pull heat away with precision,
even at 3,000 watts per accelerator.

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:59.166
Blind-mate couplings and centralized CDUs
make it easier to deploy and scale

00:00:59.166 --> 00:01:02.791
liquid-cooled systems,
making advanced cooling viable

00:01:02.791 --> 00:01:05.625
across a variety of data center sizes.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.291
To support dense, AI-ready workloads,

00:01:08.291 --> 00:01:11.291
power delivery is being reimagined
at the rack level.

00:01:11.916 --> 00:01:14.875
Power conversion
and backup systems are moving outside

00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:18.625
into external ‘sidecar’ units,
freeing up internal rack space.

00:01:19.291 --> 00:01:22.500
These sidecars feed high-voltage
DC directly into IT

00:01:22.625 --> 00:01:26.166
racks, enabling modern data centers
to adopt scalable

00:01:26.166 --> 00:01:29.208
power delivery
without full infrastructure overhauls.

00:01:29.916 --> 00:01:33.125
While direct-to-chip
cooling is now taking off, immersion

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:37.041
cooling, a radically different approach,
is also maturing and delivering

00:01:37.041 --> 00:01:40.958
two to three times
the power density of air cooling.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.333
It lowers chip temperatures
by half, and creates a stable,

00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:48.750
liquid-cooled environment that improves
system lifespan and efficiency.

00:01:49.125 --> 00:01:51.583
The Open Compute Project
is not just adapting;

00:01:51.583 --> 01:56.250
we are re-engineering the very foundations
of data center physical infrastructure.

01:56.250 --> 02:01.000
By unifying power, cooling,
and facility design through open source

02:01.000 --> 02:04.208
and standards,
we are creating the scalable, sustainable

02:04.208 --> 02:08.583
backbone for the next generation
of AI data centers.